{
 "result": "fibmod.py is built and registered. It reads n per line from stdin and prints fib(n) mod 1e9+7, using fast doubling over the bit string of n, with n reduced mod the Pisano-style period P=2(M+1), which is valid because 1e9+7 \u2261 2 (mod 5). It passed the sample in-0 (fib(10)=55) and the assay baseline is 4.207. The variant that iterates bits via bin() won +12% and was adopted. I stopped here rather than spend energy on further gains.",
